WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.002
Unpivoting raises a NULL-policy question.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.972
You can preserve rows whose value is NULL.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:09.957
That keeps the category present and marks the measurement missing.

00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:13.392
Or you can drop NULL rows after unpivoting.

00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:18.527
The right choice depends on whether missingness itself matters to the analysis.

00:00:18.527 --> 00:00:23.637
After reshaping, NULL and zero may have very different meanings.

00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:28.052
NULL can mean the category did not occur or was not measured;

00:00:28.052 --> 00:00:32.462
zero can mean it was measured and the value was truly zero.

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:38.133
Do not replace NULL with zero unless that interpretation is correct for the business question.
